Is it only me, or does it seem to anyone else that, for some
characters, things just begin getting harder and harder until... YASD?

Bob the Tourist was having a groovy time in the dungeon. Did Sokoban
and the Mines, got a lucky ?oID and got all his stuff identified, got
a supply of holy water and blessed the stuff that needed blessing. No
wishes, no DSM, one bones file (an earlier Bob) that had nothing of
note except lots of scrolls, potions, and wands. But he'd found two
more expensive camaras and was having the time of his short, happy
life getting candid shots and playing darts. "Beats hell out of
Disney," he thought.

Bob found the Quest portal when he was  XL 13. Okay, just do a bit
more exploring to gain more experience. He had some most excellent
dwarven mithril, GoP, a +4 T-Shirt, a +4 totally far out robe. With 6
points of protection, he was down (up?) to AC -21, had intrinsic
resistances to everything (except fire, and a ring to cover that), and
nothing was touching him. Life was good.

Just one thing was bothering him. He hadn't found an altar in the
whole dungeon, except the one in Minetown, and hadn't come across a
single artifact weapon. He'd gotten rather good with daggers, but he
was sort of waiting for a really good weapon to come along to channel
his skill slots into. He was making do with an elvish broadsword at
the moment, but really wanted to find a good weapon.

Finally, down on level 19, and then later on level 21, he found altars
that he quickly converted. Okay, let's get us a decent weapon! So he
sacs, and sacs, and gets clovers, and clovers, and he sacs some more,
and the bloody sacrifices keep popping off like Puff the Magic Dragon,
but nothing more comes. Owlbears, Elvenkings, titanotheres,
baluchitheria, leocrottas, and nothing appears at Bob's feet in
return. Evidently, the Lady *is* a tramp.

So by this point, Bob figures it's time to put to some good use the
blue dragon scales he'd found (actually, pulled off the carcass of the
dragon he'd beaten to death in David's Treasure Zoo). Pull out a
bottle of Rotgut '91 (a good year) and his last ?oEA. Unfortunately,
Bob had neglected to take the rest of his armor off, and thus managed
to fooproof his dwarvish helm.

So he works his way down to Medusa's level, and finds a cranky Titan
who immediately curses his BoH (that is, from blessed to uncursed).
Burdened. Back upstairs, rebless the bag with one of three HW potions
he has, and back down. Tries strumming a harp he'd found. No good.
Tries reading a scroll of taming. Doesn't faze the Titan in the
slightest (I was actually expecting at least a message like, "The
Titan resists!" but nothing). Had to beat him to death, but hey, Bob's
not complaining, rapidly climbing back to his 143 hp and pulling out
his =oLev.

Gets across the moat, whacks Medusa, and heads down. Mazes. Okay,
let's look around. Pretty soon, Bob comes across a polymorph trap.
Feeling sensitive, he avoids it. /oDig, do your stuff. Working his way
through, and wishing he hadn't stashed his eight ?oMM, he manages not
to be sensitive enough to miss a trap door, and down he is in another
maze, not knowing where either the upstairs or downstairs are. And his
only oil lamp is flickering.

Somewhere along the line, he's gotten his GoP corroded, so he's at AC
-20. Then he meets a golden naga. She casts a spell, and poof! his
robe disintegrates. Of course, since he had been sure that this was a
part of his AK, he'd had it enchanted up. Boots had gotten rusty too,
so now he's at AC -14. Zap wand of cold. Nothing happens. Zap wand of
fire. Nothing happens. Naga casts a spell again; poof! the fooproofed
dwarvish helm is gone. AC -11. Bob uses a /oTel to at least get her
away from himself while he desperately tries to find the upstairs, and
while a crazed succubus keeps asking him for his engagement ring.

Bob's mapped out most of this level now, the upstairs must be in that
small dark space, when here comes the naga again. Poof! Bob's dwarvish
mithril is gone. AC -6. Bob finally manages to find the upstairs to
Medusa's island, heads out over the moat, when an electric eel fries
his =oLev. Climbing back out onto land, he removes his dwarvish iron
shoes and puts on the boots he found in Perseus's statue. Yeah,
they'll be cursed, but Bob can take care of that once he's across the
moat. Probably can pray them off; after all his sacrificing, the Lady
owes him that much. There's a spare set of dwarvish mithril in his
stash, and plenty of helms. It'll all work out. Bob's an optimist.

Back over the moat, electric eels are shocking him again, but who
cares? Bob's shock resistant. But then, one of them wraps itself
around him, and...DYWYPI?

Yeah, I know. It's YASD. Why didn't I kill off the eels before sending
Bob over the water (like I have a dozen times before?). Or blindfold
Bob so he could see the eels and avoid them? Somehow, I'd forgotten
that electric eels could also drown you. He was up to XL 14 by now; he
could have done the Quest. He was quite survivable. But sometimes it
just seems like things get harder, and harder, and harder, and then
you're toast, one way or another.
